module cellRetentionDetection
module igG1Quantification
module cellViabilityDetection

manifest CHO_DG44_Cells
manifest CD_OptiCHO_Medium
manifest FreshMedium
manifest PBS
manifest PluronicF127
manifest TrypanBlueExclusion
manifest IgG1_Reference_Standard

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Microfluidic Cell Retention Device for Perfusion of
// Mammalian Suspension Culture
// Kwon, Prentice, De Oliveira, Madziva, Warkiani, Hamel,
// Han -- Scientific Reports 7:6703, 2017.
// DOI: 10.1038/s41598-017-06949-8
//
// Protocol: Inertial microfluidic spiral cell retention
// device for continuous perfusion culture of CHO-DG44
// cells producing human IgG1 against CD40 ligand.
// Device: PDMS spiral microchannel (600 um width,
// 80 um inner depth, 130 um outer depth, 8 loops,
// 28 uL volume). Four spiral channels combined in parallel.
// Cell retention principle: inertial focusing (F_L and F_D)
// focuses CHO cells (17.7 +/- 2.5 um diameter) near the
// inner wall -> retained via inner outlet (retentate).
// Cell-limited harvest exits via outer outlet (permeate).
// Perfusion bioreactor: 350 mL spinner flask, 2 VVD.
// Run duration: 18-25 days per bioreactor culture.
//
// NOTE ON FLOW ABSTRACTION: `mix` steps involving
// CHO_DG44_Cells model a continuous-flow peristaltic pump
// recirculation event through the spiral microchannel at
// 1 mL/min (single chip, <1.5 mL/min optimal). This is a
// BioScript abstraction for a channel-based inertial sorting
// event, not a bulk mixing step.
// Cell retention efficiency R(%) = (X_I - X_OO)/X_I x 100.
// Target: >99% at <15e6 cells/mL; ~82% at 20-23e6 cells/mL.
//
// NOTE ON IgG1 RECOVERY: Since the spiral device has no
// micro- or nanoporous membrane, IgG1 passes freely into the
// harvest stream (outer outlet). Recovery efficiency
// AR(%) = X_OO/X_I x 100 -> ~100% after Day 2 adsorption
// equilibration to tubing and fluidic adaptors.
//
// NOTE ON TEMPERATURE: All cell culture incubation steps
// run at 37 C / 5% CO2. BioScript `heat` statements model
// CO2 incubator dwell and peristaltic pump operation.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main                 -- entry: device priming,
//                               batch growth phase (4 days),
//                               perfusion initiation at 2 VVD
//   BB2  retentionPass        -- retentionSignal > 0: cell
//                               retention confirmed (R > 80%);
//                               continue perfusion sampling
//   BB3  retentionFail        -- retentionSignal <= 0: retention
//                               failure (clog or flow loss); drain
//   BB4  retentionJoin        -- join: IgG1 QC branch begins
//   BB5  igG1Pass             -- igG1Signal > 0: IgG1 detected
//                               in harvest; dispose and continue
//   BB6  igG1Fail             -- igG1Signal <= 0: product loss;
//                               drain harvest sample
//   BB7  igG1Join             -- join: viability branch begins
//   BB8  viabilityPass        -- viabilitySignal > 0: viability
//                               >97%; dispose and end
//   BB9  viabilityFail        -- viabilitySignal <= 0: viability
//                               drop (<97%); drain and end
//   BB10 finalCleanup         -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Prime the spiral microchannel device with 2%
//         Pluronic F-127 in PBS to reduce cell adhesion to
//         PDMS surfaces and equilibrate the fluidic adaptors.
//         Channel sterilised prior with 10% bleach (10 min)
//         then 70% ethanol (10 min) via peristaltic pump.
//         Device connected to sidearm ports of spinner flask
//         and harvest bottle inside a biosafety cabinet.
//         NOTE: Pluronic priming is modelled as a 5-minute
//         mix (channel equilibration dwell time).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primedChannel   = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Batch growth phase (Days 0-4, no perfusion).
//         CHO-DG44 cells inoculated at 0.3-0.4e6 cells/mL
//         into 350 mL spinner flask containing pre-warmed
//         CD OptiCHO medium. Stirring at 45 RPM.
//         Cells grown in batch mode for 4 days to establish
//         a viable exponential culture before initiating
//         perfusion. pH (7.0) and DO (40% air saturation)
//         controlled via BioFlo/CelliGen 115 or BIOSTAT A
//         bioreactor controllers.
//         400 mL pre-warmed medium transferred to flask.
//         Incubation at 37 C / 5% CO2 for 4 days (5760 min).
//
//         NOTE ON DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports s and
//         m only. 4 days = 5760 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

choCells     = dispense 1 units of CHO_DG44_Cells
batchMedium  = dispense 1 units of CD_OptiCHO_Medium
batchCulture = mix choCells with batchMedium for 5760m

heat batchCulture at 37c for 5760m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Initiate perfusion at 2 VVD (vessel volumes per
//         day) on Day 4. Fresh CD OptiCHO medium supplied
//         continuously to bioreactor via peristaltic pump.
//         Cell culture continuously recycled through the
//         4-spiral microfluidic device at 1 mL/min (single
//         chip) via a second peristaltic pump.
//         98.4% +/- 1.1% of total cells recycled back to
//         bioreactor via inner outlet (retentate).
//         Harvest solution (IgG1-containing) collected from
//         outer outlet (permeate). Harvest bottle replaced
//         daily. Working volume maintained at ~350 mL by
//         customised software (bioreactor weight control).
//         NOTE: `mix` here abstracts the spiral channel
//         inertial sorting recirculation event, not a DMF
//         electrode step. Flow rate: 1 mL/min input;
//         fluidic resistance ratio R_OO/R_IO > 2.7 set by
//         tubing diameter (510 um ID) and length.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

freshMedium      = dispense 1 units of FreshMedium
perfusionCulture = mix batchCulture with freshMedium for 10m

// Recirculate culture through spiral channel at 37 C.
// Models 18-25 day perfusion dwell at 2 VVD.
// 18 days = 25920 min (minimum run duration, Run 1).
heat perfusionCulture at 37c for 25920m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Cell retention efficiency measurement (daily QC).
//         Samples collected from bioreactor (inner outlet)
//         and harvest stream (outer outlet).
//         Cell concentration measured via BioProfile CDV
//         Analyzer (Nova Biomedical). Three aliquots per
//         sample. Max deviation 3.8% +/- 2.9% from mean.
//         R(%) = (X_I - X_OO) / X_I x 100.
//         Expected: >99% at <15e6 cells/mL;
//                   ~82% at 20-23e6 cells/mL (peak density).
//         cellRetentionDetection module abstracts the
//         automated BioProfile CDV cell concentration readout
//         comparing inner outlet vs outer outlet samples.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bioreactorSample = mix perfusionCulture with primedChannel for 2s
retentionSignal  = detect cellRetentionDetection on bioreactorSample for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Cell retention QC gate
// Pass (BB2): retentionSignal > 0 -> R > 80% confirmed,
//             device operating within spec; dispose sample
//             and continue to IgG1 branch.
// Fail (BB3): retentionSignal <= 0 -> retention failure
//             (device clogged or flow disrupted); drain
//             bioreactor sample.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (retentionJoin).
// ============================================================

if (retentionSignal > 0) {
    dispose bioreactorSample
} else {
    drain bioreactorSample
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: retentionJoin
// Dispose retention QC signal. Control falls into
// IgG1 product recovery branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose retentionSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: IgG1 product recovery measurement (daily QC).
//         IgG1 concentrations measured from bioreactor
//         (feed, X_I) and harvest stream outer outlet
//         (permeate, X_OO) by HPLC affinity chromatography
//         (Applied Biosystems 2-1001-00 column, Agilent 1100
//         Series system). Equilibration buffer: 50 mM
//         phosphate + 150 mM NaCl, pH 7.0. Elution buffer:
//         100 mM phosphate + 0.4% (v/v) phosphoric acid,
//         pH 2.5. Reference: purified IgG1-Kappa from human
//         myeloma plasma (Sigma I5154).
//         AR(%) = X_OO / X_I x 100.
//         Expected: ~80% on Days 1-2 (adsorption to tubing);
//                   ~100% from Day 3 onward.
//         Peak IgG1 in bioreactor: ~40 ug/mL after Day 9.
//         Total IgG1 yield over 18-day run: 263 mg.
//         Production rate from Day 9: 26.8 mg/day.
//         igG1Quantification module abstracts the HPLC
//         affinity chromatography antibody concentration
//         measurement on both bioreactor and harvest samples.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

harvestSample = dispense 1 units of IgG1_Reference_Standard
igG1Signal    = detect igG1Quantification on harvestSample for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: IgG1 product recovery QC gate
// Pass (BB5): igG1Signal > 0 -> IgG1 detected in harvest
//             stream at expected concentration (~100% AR);
//             dispose harvest sample and continue.
// Fail (BB6): igG1Signal <= 0 -> product loss or no signal
//             (possible retention in tubing); drain sample.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (igG1Join).
// ============================================================

if (igG1Signal > 0) {
    dispose harvestSample
} else {
    drain harvestSample
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: igG1Join
// Dispose IgG1 QC signal. Control falls into cell
// viability branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose igG1Signal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Cell viability assessment (daily QC).
//         CHO cells from bioreactor sample spread in single
//         layer on chamber slide; live cells marked by trypan
//         blue dye exclusion. 40 images from 40 different
//         fields of view per measurement. Cell diameter
//         determined by pixel distance; concentration by
//         counting (6,000 cells -> 5e6 cells/mL;
//         12,000 cells -> 10e6 cells/mL as calibrants).
//         Measurement by BioProfile FLEX and CDV Analyzers
//         (Nova Biomedical).
//         Long-term biocompatibility confirmed: CHO cells
//         processed continuously for >145 h at 1 mL/min
//         with average retention efficiency 98% (1.6% range)
//         and NO significant decrease in viability (n=3).
//         Target viability: >97% throughout perfusion culture
//         (99% +/- 1%, mean +/- s.d., n=9 after Day 10).
//         cellViabilityDetection module abstracts the trypan
//         blue exclusion viability readout.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

viabilitySample  = dispense 1 units of CHO_DG44_Cells
trypanStain      = dispense 1 units of TrypanBlueExclusion
stainedViability = mix viabilitySample with trypanStain for 2m

viabilitySignal  = detect cellViabilityDetection on stainedViability for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Cell viability QC gate
// Pass (BB8): viabilitySignal > 0 -> cell viability >97%,
//             biocompatibility confirmed; dispose stained
//             sample and end experiment successfully.
// Fail (BB9): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> viability drop below
//             threshold (possible shear damage or device
//             fouling); drain stained sample and end.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedViability
} else {
    drain stainedViability
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose viability QC signal; experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
